    "narrative": "LawDog enters the 2026-06-23 slate with a balanced offensive outlook, led by **Luis Arraez**, who earns today\u2019s highest efficiency score of 68.87. Despite a minor penalty for unfavorable BvP history against Civale, **Luis Arraez**\u2019s leadoff positioning and the favorable SP skill rating make him our anchor. **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.25) and **Taylor Ward** (63.91) also stand out as elite starts; **Taylor Ward** leverages a prime leadoff spot against Johnson\u2019s high-xERA profile, while **Jung Hoo Lee** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against Civale, showcasing the high-floor production we need to maintain our competitive standing. **Cal Raleigh** (63.77) provides our most significant SP skill value add (+11%) today, making him an essential start behind the plate as he targets Keller.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Drew Gilbert**, who remained on the bench with a 53.80 score. While **Drew Gilbert** projects as a capable option, he was pushed out by the high-ceiling platoon advantages presented by **Daulton Varsho** and **Gavin Sheets**, both of whom benefit significantly from facing right-handed pitching today. We are playing it safe with **Yainer Diaz** (48.97), whose score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Bieber; while his raw output remains marginal, he stays in the lineup to ensure we don't bleed too much value in our daily efficiency targets. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Dylan Beavers**, as their absence due to injury remains a significant drag on our overall team-wide scoring ceiling. With no major weather concerns reported, we are locked in to capitalize on these mid-rotation matchups.",
